From 8f83a6054e5866b1019da58548f92d7e5f13f29e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 21:05:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] platform/arm64: add Yoga Slim 7x IT8987 EC driver + DT
 node

Backport of Maya Matuszczyk's posted series 'qcom-x1e-it8987'
(lore.kernel.org/lkml/Z2W_A5xewTC2ZJFs@linaro.org), taken from the
CadmiumLinux/kernel packaging of it. Adds i2c5 + embedded-controller@76
(tlmm gpio66 IRQ) to the Slim 7x DT and a small i2c driver that notifies
the EC of screen-off/suspend-enter (reg 0x23, values 0x03/0x01) and the
reverse on resume.

On this machine the EC owns the keyboard backlight, so this is what
turns it off during suspend -- there is no host-side control path.
Mainline has since gained Qualcomm's own variant (qcom-hamoa-ec,
compatible qcom,hamoa-crd-ec) using the same register 0x23, but it
targets reference devices and does not send the screen-off notify.
Local Makefile hunk adjusted (7.1 has more entries).

Applies to EL1 and EL2 boots alike (base board DTS).
